# Static err() coverage: band label + range, chart id, bundle members, and
# the DELETED `chart level=` (`CHART-LEVEL-KEY`)
#
# 0.3 (`SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`): this fixture was ONE `figdown 0.1 topology` section
# until this release, and the ruling splits it in two, because the three
# constructs it covers no longer share a genre: `band` was WITHDRAWN from
# `topology` (there a BAND is a frequency band) and `bundle` was WITHDRAWN
# from `block` (there it is a ring round parallel edges with nothing to
# name). It is split into two SECTIONS of one file rather than two fixtures:
# the subject is a set of static argument errors, not a genre, and one of the
# halves would otherwise be a fixture of a single line. Multi-section (`MULTI-FIGURE-DOCUMENTS`) is
# the device this suite already uses when one fixture has to span genres —
# `224-flowchart-roles-genre-scoped` writes four headers, `265` two.
# `chart` goes with `band` in the `block` section: it is a `GENRE-COMPOSITION` REGION OPENER,
# declared by every scene genre, so either section could host it.
figdown 0.1 block
node a "A"
band "z" in=a
chart
chart t level=-1
figdown 0.1 topology
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a -- b
bundle empty
